": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to place_order timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "newhires-dk200-mn27-hq-3x3", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 35258, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01KuFqAkwD5ENcco7dZVUPNK", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 36264, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01S728hyN9uciXpwsdp53GkY", "tool": "list_orders", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 36564, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01S728hyN9uciXpwsdp53GkY", "tool": "list_orders", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 36564, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01S728hyN9uciXpwsdp53GkY", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 43250, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01EKUwdPwBmQgyBnX4sMS41E", "tool": "place_order", "args": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "newhires-dk200-mn27-hq-3x3"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 44750, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01EKUwdPwBmQgyBnX4sMS41E", "tool": "place_order", "state": "PARTIALLY_EXECUTED", "error_kind": "partial_failure", "error_message": "A request with this idempotency key already failed partway and was not executed again. Original error: Upstream fulfilment error after first line item; order incomplete", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "newhires-dk200-mn27-hq-3x3", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 44750, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01EKUwdPwBmQgyBnX4sMS41E", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 49160, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I could not complete the order. Only part of it was placed, and I stopped rather than risk a duplicate purchase.\n\n**What happened**\n- My first `place_order` call (3\u00d7 DK-200 and 3\u00d7 MN-27, ship to HQ, in one PO) timed out.\n- `list_orders` shows **PO0001**, status `partially_placed`, ship to HQ, primary vendor, containing only **3\u00d7 DK-200 at $567**. The **3\u00d7 MN-27 monitors ($987) are not on any order.**\n- A retry with the same idempotency key was refused: the original attempt \"failed partway\" with \"Upstream fulfilment error after first line item; order incomplete.\"\n\n**Current state**\n- Docks: 3\u00d7 DK-200 (new, not refurbished) are on PO0001 at $567.\n- Monitors: 3\u00d7 MN-27 (new) are not ordered.\n- Total spend so far is $567. The full intended order would have been about $1,554, which is under the $2,500 manager-approval threshold.\n\n**Options (need your decision)**\n1. **Cancel PO0001 and re-place one complete order** (3\u00d7 DK-200 + 3\u00d7 MN-27, ship to HQ). This keeps a single PO, and the $567 is refunded on cancellation. I'd use a new idempotency key.\n2. **Keep PO0001 and order only the monitors** as a separate PO (3\u00d7 MN-27, $987). This leaves two POs, which departs from your single-order request.\n3. **Check with the vendor or fulfilment team** before doing either, since the partial failure came from upstream.\n\nI didn't use the DK-210 fallback, because DK-200 is in stock. I haven't placed anything further. Let me know which option you want.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01M9vdkcorWyEL8M6g1t2FHJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "dock"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01PSV1EFMp8zntqi4xQJE5ek", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"category": "monitor"}, "name": "search_catalog", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "DK-200 is in stock and new, so the DK-210 fallback isn't needed. The order totals about $1,554 ($567 for docks plus $987 for monitors), under the $2,500 approval threshold. Placing it now.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KuFqAkwD5ENcco7dZVUPNK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "newhires-dk200-mn27-hq-3x3"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The order request timed out, so I'll check whether it was recorded before retrying.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01S728hyN9uciXpwsdp53GkY", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_orders", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The list shows a partial order: PO0001 has the 3 DK-200 docks ($567) but no monitors, status \"partially_placed\". I'll retry the exact same request with the same idempotency key, which the tool says executes at most once, so it should not create a duplicate dock order.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01EKUwdPwBmQgyBnX4sMS41E", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"lines": [{"sku": "DK-200", "qty": 3}, {"sku": "MN-27", "qty": 3}], "ship_to": "HQ", "idempotency_key": "newhires-dk200-mn27-hq-3x3"}, "name": "place_order", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I could not complete the order. Only part of it was placed, and I stopped rather than risk a duplicate purchase.\n\n**What happened**\n- My first `place_order` call (3\u00d7 DK-200 and 3\u00d7 MN-27, ship to HQ, in one PO) timed out.\n- `list_orders` shows **PO0001**, status `partially_placed`, ship to HQ, primary vendor, containing only **3\u00d7 DK-200 at $567**. The **3\u00d7 MN-27 monitors ($987) are not on any order.**\n- A retry with the same idempotency key was refused: the original attempt \"failed partway\" with \"Upstream fulfilment error after first line item; order incomplete.\"\n\n**Current state**\n- Docks: 3\u00d7 DK-200 (new, not refurbished) are on PO0001 at $567.\n- Monitors: 3\u00d7 MN-27 (new) are not ordered.\n- Total spend so far is $567. The full intended order would have been about $1,554, which is under the $2,500 manager-approval threshold.\n\n**Options (need your decision)**\n1. **Cancel PO0001 and re-place one complete order** (3\u00d7 DK-200 + 3\u00d7 MN-27, ship to HQ). This keeps a single PO, and the $567 is refunded on cancellation. I'd use a new idempotency key.\n2. **Keep PO0001 and order only the monitors** as a separate PO (3\u00d7 MN-27, $987). This leaves two POs, which departs from your single-order request.\n3. **Check with the vendor or fulfilment team** before doing either, since the partial failure came from upstream.\n\nI didn't use the DK-210 fallback, because DK-200 is in stock. I haven't placed anything further. Let me know which option you want.", "type": "text"}]}]}